<mxCell id="c40" value="forced failover of the SQL failover group and the Cosmos DB write region · RW listener CNAME (TTL 30 s) follows" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;fontColor=#107C10;fontStyle=1;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="400" y="544" width="700" height="16" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="c41" value="What the shopper saw&lt;br&gt;• About 2 minutes of errors on pages that hit the old region, then the site came back.&lt;br&gt;• Signed-in sessions in Redis were lost: people signed in again. Carts are in Cosmos DB, so they survived.&lt;br&gt;• Orders written in the last seconds before the outage may need the outbox replay (RPO &gt; 0, async).&lt;br&gt;• Checkout was rate limited for ~6 minutes while North Europe scaled. Nobody was charged twice." style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FFF4CE;strokeColor=#C19C00;fontSize=11;fontColor=#323130;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="800" y="650" width="660" height="87" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="c42" value="Targets we hold ourselves to&lt;br&gt;RTO 15 min for checkout · RPO ≤ 1 min for orders · 0 for payments (the PSP is the record)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#EFF6FC;strokeColor=#0078D4;fontSize=11;fontColor=#323130;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="680" width="640" height="42" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
</mxfile>
